            {
              "text": "When looking for consultancies in Hobart to assist with business workflow automation and Microsoft Power Automate implementation, the market features a mix of **established Tasmanian-headquartered IT consultancies** and **national Microsoft Solutions Partners** with dedicated local offices:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Top Tasmanian & Hobart-Headquartered Consultancies\n\n* **Intuit Technologies**\n  * **Overview:** One of Tasmania’s largest and most prominent IT service providers and consultancies, with long-standing offices in Hobart and Launceston. \n  * **Power Automate / Workflow Fit:** Intuit has a dedicated Microsoft Cloud & Business Applications practice. They assist organisations with Dynamics 365, Microsoft 365, and the Microsoft Power Platform (Power Automate, Power Apps, Dataverse). They are particularly well-suited for mid-market to enterprise-level process automation, approval workflows, and systems integration.\n* **ISW (Information Symbiosis Worldwide)**\n  * **Overview:** Founded and headquartered in Hobart, ISW has operated for over 25 years as a technology consultancy and custom software provider.\n  * **Power Automate / Workflow Fit:** ISW specializes in modern workplace solutions and digital transformation. They build workflow automations and internal apps connecting SharePoint, Microsoft Teams, and the wider Power Platform. They are an ideal choice if your automation involves document management, legacy software modernization, or custom web integration.\n* **Element Digital / Tempus Innovative Solutions**\n  * **Overview:** Local Hobart-based consulting firms geared toward SMEs, non-profits, and government agencies seeking practical digital transformation.\n  * **Power Automate / Workflow Fit:** They focus on process discovery, replacing repetitive administrative paper/spreadsheet tasks, and orchestrating workflows using Power Automate, Logic Apps, and Cloud APIs.\n\n---\n\n### 2. National Partners with a Strong Hobart Presence\n\n* **Data#3 (Hobart Office)**\n  * **Overview:** One of Australia’s largest Microsoft Tier-1 Solutions Partners with a local team and office in Hobart.\n  * **Power Automate / Workflow Fit:** Data#3 possesses deep expertise across Microsoft Business Applications, Power Platform, Copilot Studio, and Robotic Process Automation (RPA). They are suited for larger mid-market, government (Tasmanian State Government / councils), or education deployments that require stringent security, enterprise governance, and complex multi-system orchestrations.\n* **MYtech Consulting Services (Hobart Office)**\n  * **Overview:** Located on Macquarie Street in Hobart, MYtech is a Microsoft Solutions Partner focusing on modern work and business systems.\n  * **Power Automate / Workflow Fit:** Their core services specifically emphasize Microsoft Dynamics 365 and the Power Platform suite (Power Apps, Power Automate, and Power BI) to automate administrative bottlenecks, client tracking, and finance workflows.\n\n---\n\n### Which Consultancy to Pick?\n\n| Your Need | Recommended Path |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Full-service IT + Power Platform adoption** | **Intuit Technologies** – Great balance of local Tasmanian support, managed IT, and dedicated Microsoft business application teams. |\n| **Workplace collaboration & custom integration** | **ISW** – Best if your automations tie deeply into SharePoint document sets, custom portals, or hybrid environments. |\n| **Enterprise-scale governance & compliance** | **Data#3** – Best if you have complex data policies, large license footprints, or require a Power Platform **Center of Excellence (CoE)** setup. |\n| **Boutique SME process transformation** | **Tempus** or **MYtech** – Best for targeted projects needing hands-on workflow mapping and rapid deployment. |\n\n---\n\n### Key Questions to Ask When Engaging:\n1. **Licensing & Connectors:** Will the automations run on standard *seeded* Microsoft 365 licensing, or will they require premium Power Automate / Dataverse per-flow or per-user licenses?\n2. **Environment & ALM Strategy:** How do they manage environments (Dev/Test/Prod) and solution packaging to ensure workflows don't break when individual staff accounts change?\n3. **Training & Handover:** Do they build \"black box\" solutions, or will they upskill your internal team to maintain and update basic flows moving forward?",
